; One rule per period expression hledger 1.52 accepts, over a pinned Jan-Jun
; 2026 span. The grammar in `parse::parse_period_spec` was inferred from the
; CLI, and the only defensible proof that our occurrences match hledger's is
; hledger's own output over this file -- see tests/budget_golden.rs.
;
; The three forms hledger itself REJECTS (`every last day of month`,
; `every 15th,last day of month`, `every jan`) are deliberately absent. hledger
; refuses to read a file containing one, so it cannot be an oracle for them and
; a golden could not be generated at all. That they degrade to a locked rule
; rather than failing the whole journal is asserted directly in parse.rs, by
; `hledger_rejects_degrade_rather_than_failing_the_journal`, which is the only
; place that claim can be made.
;
; Every goal is an unbalanced-virtual `(account)` posting and every account is
; distinct, so each row of the golden reads as exactly one rule's occurrences.

; -- the five fixed intervals, and the synonyms that mean one of them ---------

~ monthly  simple monthly
    (expenses:rent)  $100

~ every month  every-month synonym
    (expenses:phone)  $30

; A rule header carries a comment and tags, which the parser used to discard.
~ monthly  tagged rule  ; growth: 3%/yr, scenario: base
    (expenses:insurance)  $50

; -- multipliers -------------------------------------------------------------

~ every 2 weeks  fortnightly pay
    (income:salary)  $-1000

~ biweekly  biweekly synonym
    (expenses:groceries)  $200

; -- anchored forms ----------------------------------------------------------

~ every 15th day of month  anchored day of month
    (expenses:gym)  $40

~ every 3rd tuesday of month  anchored weekday of month
    (expenses:therapy)  $150

~ every tuesday  anchored weekday
    (expenses:coffee)  $10

; -- bounds: `from` is a phase anchor, `to` is EXCLUSIVE ---------------------

~ quarterly from 2026-04-01  bounded quarterly
    (expenses:auto)  $300

~ monthly from 2026-03-01 to 2026-05-01  bounded monthly
    (expenses:tutoring)  $250

~ every 2 months from 2026-02-01  multiplied and bounded
    (expenses:haircut)  $60

; -- one-offs, and a rule that never fires in this span ----------------------

~ 2026-04-15  a single occurrence
    (expenses:taxprep)  $400

~ every 12/25  annual, outside the span
    (expenses:gifts)  $500

; -- actuals, so the report is not all zeroes --------------------------------

2026-01-05 groceries
    expenses:groceries   $180.00
    assets:checking

2026-02-17 therapy
    expenses:therapy     $150.00
    assets:checking

2026-03-20 parking
    expenses:parking      $12.00
    assets:checking
